Invoke the process with command `python dv_handoff_main.py --serve --port 9090`














FOLDERS:

src/ : Contains code files for the agents
db/ : Contains code files for the database manager
logs/ : Stores logging files for the application
managers/models/ : Contains code files for the model manager
server/ : Contains code files for the application API server
utils/ : Contains utility code for the agents
docs/ : Stores documentation


MCP CONFIGURATION (stored in mcp_config.py):

MCP_CONFIG stores the MCP-related details for MCP servers. It is a list of MCP servers, identified by:
- Server Name : Type of MCP server (e.g. "mysql", "duckdb")
- Server details : Server URL or command-line arguments to run MCP server

Below parameters are specific to Database MCPs
- Query Function name : MCP Function responsible for executing queries
- Query key : The placeholder to be sent as key, in request to MCP server

Example:

MCP_CONFIG={
    "mysql":{
        "server":{
                "transport": "http",  # HTTP-based remote server
                # Ensure you start your weather server on port 8000
                "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp",
            },
        "query_function": "run_query",
        "query_key": "query",
    },
    "duckdb":{
        "server": {
                "command": "uvx",
                "args": ["mcp-server-motherduck", "--db-path", "./data/duckdb/traffic.db",
                         "--max-rows", "10000", "--max-chars", "1000000"],
                         #"--max-rows", "100000", "--max-chars", "10000000"],
                "transport": "stdio"
            },
        "query_function": "execute_query",
        "query_key": "sql",
    },
}

New MCP servers need to be added to this config list, to become available for use.
Relevant MCP details can be added, based on code requirements.



WORKING WITH GPUs
## Reference : https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-18-run-nvidia-gpu-containers-podman/view




PODMAN CREATE COMMANDS
podman run -d --name redis-stack --memory 1g --memory-reservation 500m -p 6380:6379 -p 8001:8001 -v ./user_store/redis/storage:/data:Z redis/redis-stack

podman run -d --name pg-chkptr --memory 1g --memory-reservation 500m -p 5433:5432 -e POSTGRES_USER=checkpointer -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=checkpointer -e POSTGRES_DB=checkpointer -v ./session_memory/postgres/storage:/var/lib/postgresql/data:Z docker.io/library/postgres:16


podman run -d --name ollama-gpu-pod -e OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=4 -e OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=1 -e OLLAMA_MAX_QUEUE=16 --cdi-spec-dir=/home/Vegayan2/.config/cdi --security-opt=label=disable --device nvidia.com/gpu=all --memory 15g --memory-reservation 10g -p 11437:11434 -v /var/lib/ollama/storage_pods/1:/root/.ollama:Z docker.io/ollama/ollama:latest

podman run -d --name ollama-gpu-pod-1 -e OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=4 -e OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=1 -e OLLAMA_MAX_QUEUE=16 --cdi-spec-dir=/home/Vegayan2/.config/cdi --security-opt=label=disable --device nvidia.com/gpu=all --memory 15g --memory-reservation 10g -p 11438:11434 -v /var/lib/ollama/storage_pods/2:/root/.ollama:Z docker.io/ollama/ollama:latest

podman run -d --name ollama-gpu-pod-2 -e OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=2 -e OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=2 -e OLLAMA_MAX_QUEUE=16 --cdi-spec-dir=/home/Vegayan2/.config/cdi --security-opt=label=disable --device nvidia.com/gpu=all --memory 15g --memory-reservation 10g -p 11436:11434 -v /var/lib/ollama/storage:/root/.ollama:z docker.io/ollama/ollama:latest

podman run -d --name ollama-gpu-pod-3 -e OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=2 -e OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=2 -e OLLAMA_MAX_QUEUE=16 --cdi-spec-dir=/home/Vegayan2/.config/cdi --security-opt=label=disable --device nvidia.com/gpu=all --memory 15g --memory-reservation 10g -p 11435:11434 -v /var/lib/ollama/storage:/root/.ollama:z docker.io/ollama/ollama:latest

podman run -d --name ollama-gpu-pod-4 -e OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=2 -e OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=2 -e OLLAMA_MAX_QUEUE=16 --cdi-spec-dir=/home/Vegayan2/.config/cdi --security-opt=label=disable --device nvidia.com/gpu=all --memory 15g --memory-reservation 10g -p 11439:11434 -v /var/lib/ollama/storage:/root/.ollama:z docker.io/ollama/ollama:latest


podman run -d --name qdrant-cpu -p 6335:6333 -p 6336:6334 -v /var/lib/ollama/qdrant/storage/cpu:/qdrant/storage:Z docker.io/qdrant/qdrant:latest

podman run -d --name qdrant-gpu --device nvidia.com/gpu=all --security-opt=label=disable -v /var/lib/ollama/qdrant/storage/gpu:/qdrant/storage:Z -p 6337:6333 -p 6338:6334 -e QDRANT__GPU__INDEXING=1 qdrant/qdrant:gpu-nvidia-latest